\b Global Sports ID Current Security Status\b0\par
\par
\b Current status:\b0\par
The app now has strong security protections across the app, database, backups, and release setup.\par
\par
\b 1. Backups and project safety\b0\par
- Project pushed to GitHub on the clean main branch.\par
- Local project folder still exists.\par
- Full backup folder exists: C:\Global\GlobalSportsID-FullBackup\par
- Source zip backup exists.\par
- Git bundle backup exists.\par
- .env is no longer tracked on the pushed branch.\par
\par
\b 2. Supabase database security\b0\par
- Row Level Security enabled on core tables.\par
- FORCE RLS enabled on core tables.\par
- Policies created for profiles, contact requests, trials, offers, conversations, conversation members, and messages.\par
- Same-sport access enforced for profiles, trials, offers, and communication.\par
- Users can only update their own profile.\par
- Coaches can only manage their own trials and offers.\par
- Only conversation members can read messages and conversations.\par
- Only valid participants can update contact requests.\par
\par
\b 3. Database validation and integrity rules\b0\par
- Profile sport cannot be changed after registration.\par
- Player profiles require full name, sport, gender, age, and position.\par
- Coach profiles require full name, sport, and team.\par
- Email format is validated in the database.\par
- Invalid ages are rejected.\par
- Contact requests to self are blocked.\par
- Cross-sport contact requests are blocked.\par
- Trial and offer sport must match the coach profile sport.\par
- Empty messages are blocked.\par
- Conversations are limited to two members.\par
- Duplicate direct conversations between the same two users are blocked.\par
\par
\b 4. Authentication security\b0\par
- Email signup is enabled.\par
- Anonymous sign-in is disabled.\par
- Manual linking is disabled.\par
- Email confirmation is enabled.\par
- App signup flow updated to support email confirmation properly.\par
- Duplicate email registration now shows: Email already registered.\par
\par
\b 5. App behavior protections\b0\par
- Wrong account type login is blocked.\par
- Sport-based separation is enforced in app and database.\par
- Coaches contact players directly.\par
- Players request coaches first.\par
- Only accepted request flows become active conversations.\par
- Unread message state is tracked.\par
\par
\b 6. Release configuration safety\b0\par
- iOS bundle ID set: com.globalsportsid.app\par
- Android package set: com.globalsportsid.app\par
- Dark splash/background aligned with the app branding.\par
- Expo package mismatch warning fixed.\par
- SafeAreaView migrated to the supported safe-area package.\par
\par
\b 7. What still should be kept secure manually\b0\par
- Keep .env private.\par
- Never expose the Supabase service role key in the app.\par
- Turn on 2FA for GitHub, Supabase, Apple Developer, and Google Play.\par
- Keep USB and offline backups private because they include .env.\par
- Keep testing with real accounts before launch.\par
\par
\b 8. Recommended final checks before launch\b0\par
- Test a brand-new signup with email confirmation.\par
- Test duplicate email signup.\par
- Test player to coach request flow.\par
- Test coach to player direct messaging.\par
- Test cross-sport blocking.\par
- Test logout and fresh login.\par
- Test on Android emulator and real phone.\par
- Test a production build before store submission.\par
\par
\b Summary\b0\par
The app is now in a much stronger security state than before. The most important protections are active in the database, the project is backed up, and the app authentication flow is safer for launch.\par
